# Termius quick import — SSH Config format
# Import: Hosts → New Host dropdown → Import → SSH Config
#
# Termius import is LOSSY: only Host/HostName/User carry reliably.
# IdentityFile imports only in desktop builds from termius.com (not store builds).
# RemoteCommand/keepalives are NOT imported — don't rely on them.
#
# After import:
#   1. Re-attach your key in Termius Keychain (or paste password).
#   2. Create these snippets (name → command):
#        herdr attach        → herdr                              (startup snippet for this host)
#        herdr status        → herdr status
#        herdr agents        → herdr agent list
#        herdr read agent    → herdr agent read <name> --tail 100
#        herdr stop server   → herdr server stop                  (after updates; kills panes)
#        herdr reload config → herdr server reload-config
#        herdr session       → herdr session attach <name>
#   3. Set "herdr attach" as this host's Startup Snippet.
#   4. "herdr-shell" stays snippet-free for plain shell access.
#
# Usage: SSH in → snippet runs herdr → ctrl+b q detaches (session survives);
# reconnect reattaches to your agents. iOS may drop the connection after
# ~20-30s in background; the herdr server keeps panes running regardless.

Host herdr
    HostName YOUR_SERVER_IP_OR_DOMAIN
    User YOUR_USERNAME
    # IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519

Host herdr-shell
    HostName YOUR_SERVER_IP_OR_DOMAIN
    User YOUR_USERNAME
    # IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
